cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Clustered Safety Events and the Effective Sample Size in
  Autonomous Vehicle Fleet Rate Estimation
authors:
  - family-names: "Emami Tabrizi"
    given-names: "Pouria"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/pouriaetab/av-clustered-rates"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22646556
keywords:
  - autonomous vehicles
  - safety validation
  - design effect
  - effective sample size
  - clustered data
  - rare event estimation
abstract: >-
  Autonomous vehicle fleet validation estimates rare-event rates per mile and
  attaches confidence statements to them, treating logged events as independent
  Poisson arrivals. Real fleet events arrive in clusters. Modelling the event
  stream as a compound Poisson process shows that ignoring this inflates the
  variance of the rate estimator by a design effect, so nominal confidence
  intervals under-cover and required demonstration mileage is understated. The
  correction substitutes an effective sample size estimated from the logs
  themselves.
